{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 38, :comments ["<b>And they shall make for themselves tzitzit</b> The Holy One, blessed be He, said: I desire that you be wrapped like angels, clad in linen garments, and just as you saw Me wrapped, therefore He commanded tekhelet, which resembles the firmament and the Throne of Glory:" "<b>ציצית</b> In the atbash reversal, in gematria it equals כסאי (My throne):" "<b>ציצית</b> In gematria: צדקות (righteousness), and in gematria: נשרים (eagles) — to say that whoever is scrupulous in the commandment of tzitzit merits and sees the face of the Shekhinah, as written: \"In righteousness I shall behold Your face,\" and merits what is stated: \"and I will bear you on eagles' wings.\""], :book :numbers, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:22:18.797266370Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}